Z||000000||DisfourDan||06-21-2001||09:21 PM||||Hey guys, The fiero I am looking at has a slight exhaust leak, now if the car has not yet been fixed by pontiacs recall, I could have them fix it because of the parts they put on the car.  Here is the info I obtained from Ogre's cave  <P>1984, 85, 86<BR>New exhaust manifold, heat stove, New dipstick, 5 head bolts, exhaust manifold shield (between manifold and block), new O2 sensor, heat reflective tape for wires, and additional collaterals needed to install main parts (nuts bolts clamps etc.).<P>Is this true?  This would mean that the exhaust leak would be fixed, and it would pass its smog test.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DJRice||06-21-2001||09:33 PM||||Recalls dont expire, so if the recall work has not been done to that car then GM is responsible for it.  <P>Your local pontiac service department can run your VIN number and tell you if the recall was performed.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-21-2001||09:34 PM||||Some dealerships will still do the recall's and some won't. As for passing emissions, Odd's are you can just do a tune-up and some injector cleaner to pass the test. If you find a dealer to do the recall's you can have them check emissions for you.||||reg||1
