Z||000015||Kevin-84SE||06-22-2001||03:09 PM||||I would recommend you check the NHTSA web site to see what recalls have been issued for your car and then call your dealer and ask that they tell you when the recall work was done. They probably will not be able to tell you. From What I have been told the Database the dealer uses does not go back that far. If your car has evidence that the recall work was not done then you should demand that they do the recall work.  <BR>I went through a battle with a dealer and Pontiac back in December and they finally agreed to do the recall on the e-brake of my 84 Fiero. I know the recall was not done because I have had the car since new I still have the recall notice and card that is supposed to be filled out when completed. I also know that my car has not been to a dealer or anywhere for service since 1989. I have not had a chance to schedule it yet but I hope they don't give me a hard time. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||dlancer407||06-22-2001||03:36 PM||||Hi everyone; I just bought a 1985 V6 Fiero GT myself. I to have a small exhaust manifold leak on my car. I found the recall on the Michigan Fiero web site for my car. It is( Product Safety Campaign-88-C-24 )you can print it out it is 12 pages long.It covers 1985-88 Fiero models with 2.8L V6 Engines (RPO L44 ). I went to two Pontiac dealers ( I live in Cincinnati Ohio ) The first one told me that his computer would only go back Ten years on VIN numbers. The second dealer I talked to ran my Vin # and it also came back no open recall on my car. I then got Pontiac Customer Service 1-800 number off Pontiac's web site. I called and talked to a very nice lady who took my number and said she would try and look up my Vin # and call me back. She called about an hour later. She could not find any info on my car. She then gave me a customer request # and told me to go to the dealer and have them visually inspect the car and see if the work had been done.I did that and the Tech said it did not look like it had been done. One giveaway that the work has not been done is THE RUBBER SEAL ON THE BACK DECK LID IS REMOVED AS PART OF THE RECALL. if your car still has it on there like mine did the recall probably has not been done.The dealer then ordered the kit for the 85 model which includes the exhaust manifold. The part number is 10154785. They called Monday the parts are in and my car goes in next Thursday to have the work done. If your car is an 85 the VIN # runs from FP200001 thru FP276370 If yours fall in that range it has been recalled. The bulletin also states that if the dealer does not fix the car in a reasonable amount of time you should contact NHTSA. It also states that ( DEALERS ARE TO SERVICE ALL VEHICLES SUBJECT TO THIS CAMPAIGN AT NO CHARGE TO OWNERS, REGARDLESS OF MILEAGE, AGE OF VEHICLE, OR OWNERSHIP, FROM THIS TIME FORWARD.) So I don't think any dealer can refuse to do the work. I know this post is long but I hope it helps. ||||reg||1
Z||000017||DisfourDan||06-22-2001||04:22 PM||||Is your Fiero 1985 GT a 2.8L? or a 2.5L?||||reg||1
Z||000018||dlancer407||06-22-2001||07:55 PM||||Mine is a V6 2.8lit. automatic. The recall notice does not say it is for automatic or stick. It covers all cars that fall in the range of the VIN# I provided in my last post. ||||reg||7
